1
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:11,844
Your Honor.

2
00:00:11,845 --> 00:00:14,054
The plaintiff was to receive land

3
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:16,306
as a gift on the special condition
that she marry.

4
00:00:16,307 --> 00:00:17,975
The defendant knew this.

5
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:19,143
Therefore, she seeks

6
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:22,271
3.3 billion yen in damages,
equivalent to the value of the land

7
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:25,065
she would have received,
but for the defendant's negligence.

8
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:26,025
What are you doing?

9
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,779
I was imitating my boss.

10
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:32,031
Do you have a party act coming up?

11
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,323
No.

12
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:35,909
My boss said something to me recently.

13
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:39,246
That... depends on

14
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:42,583
what kind of lawyer
you want to be, doesn't it?

15
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:46,044
The only lawyers I know
are my boss and colleagues.

16
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:49,173
First, I decided to become a lawyer
like my boss, Mr. Miyaji,

17
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:50,215
so I was imitating him.

18
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:52,135
Is he someone you look up to?

19
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,513
I don't know.

20
00:00:56,097 --> 00:00:58,223
He can't stand up to the managing partner,

21
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:01,643
<i>but he pays close attention
to new lawyers like me.</i>

22
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:04,563
I feel I can rely on him
when it really matters.

23
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:05,981
Sounds like a good boss.

24
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:09,319
But being a lawyer like my colleagues
might be nice too.

25
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:12,362
Ever since our legal training, Ms. Asahi

26
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:15,282
<i>has protected me from being made fun of.</i>

27
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:17,452
<i>She is cheerful and considerate,</i>

28
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:20,580
and as warm as the spring sunshine.

29
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:26,502
My other colleague, Mr. Himi,
sometimes says unkind things to me,

30
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:27,878
<i>but he is very ambitious.</i>

31
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:30,756
<i>He calculates what he needs to do
and acts accordingly.</i>

32
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:33,258
He has qualities that I don't possess.

33
00:01:33,259 --> 00:01:37,221
You know, Minami,
I used to want to be a lawyer myself.

34
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:39,891
I had to give it up for various reasons,

35
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,059
but if I'd become one,

36
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:45,771
maybe I could have been
someone for you to look up to.

37
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:46,730
You, Dad?

38
00:01:46,731 --> 00:01:47,981
Yeah.

39
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:49,442
Objection!

40
00:01:50,318 --> 00:01:53,947
When you spoke
to the defendant on the phone,

41
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:57,199
he said he'd hit his boss with a vase.

42
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,826
That's what you heard?

43
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:02,287
Now, striking someone
on the head with a vase

44
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:04,248
could indeed prove fatal.

45
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:07,668
However, the defendant's actual weapon

46
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:09,419
wasn't a vase.

47
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,840
It was a vest!

48
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:16,010
Huh? Minami?

49
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:18,179
Minami!

50
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:27,188
I'm sorry.

51
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,125
Excuse me.

52
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:51,170
May I ask you something?

53
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:55,383
Please wait a moment.

54
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:02,640
What's wrong?

55
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:07,437
It's gone...

56
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:09,063
It's gone!

57
00:03:24,996 --> 00:03:26,622
Ms. Minamida.

58
00:03:26,623 --> 00:03:29,041
Good morning, Mr. Miyaji.

59
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:32,545
I'm looking for my whale, Humpy,
so I can't spare a moment.

60
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:36,506
Incidentally, the name Humpy

61
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,634
comes from the English "humpback whale"...

62
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:41,346
Hey, is this the Humpy you're looking for?

63
00:03:41,971 --> 00:03:43,555
Humpy!

64
00:03:43,556 --> 00:03:46,225
A kid outside said he'd found it
and gave it to me.

65
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:48,895
What a relief. Thank you very much.

66
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:51,481
So you found your Bambi, then?

67
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:52,940
It's Humpy.

68
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:54,149
Mr. Motojima!

69
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:55,067
It's Humpy.

70
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,151
No, no.

71
00:03:56,152 --> 00:03:59,030
This gentleman was my mentor
during legal training.

72
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:00,697
I see...

73
00:04:00,698 --> 00:04:02,908
You were Mr. Miyaji's mentor.

74
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:05,662
It's been such a long time.

75
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:07,997
You haven't changed a bit.

76
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:13,961
My doctor says I'm getting too old
and should cut back on...

77
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:15,379
That... What was it?

78
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,422
That... You know, that...

79
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:18,967
- Overindulging?
- No.

80
00:04:22,095 --> 00:04:23,179
Trials.

81
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:26,391
He says to cut back on trials.

82
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:31,687
Which brings me to a favor
I'd like to ask, Miyaji.

83
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:36,943
I'd like you to take over
a case I'm handling.

84
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:42,240
- This is the one.
- Yes.

85
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:46,286
A suit to revoke urban
planning project approval?

86
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:53,000
I've been handling disputes
in Tanegi Village for 50 years.

87
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:55,794
Now they're building a railway through it.

88
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:57,130
YANOHARA, TANEKI, TAKAMAKI

89
00:04:57,714 --> 00:05:00,966
Even once the line opens,

90
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:03,468
The village won't benefit from it.

91
00:05:03,469 --> 00:05:04,386
Exactly.

92
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:08,140
This route was selected
after several experts reviewed it.

93
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:12,060
It'll be very hard to change the route
now that it's been decided.

94
00:05:12,061 --> 00:05:14,647
Have they offered
the residents compensation?

95
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:18,567
A suitable amount might help
persuade them to agree.

96
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:22,237
Land is cheap throughout this whole area.

97
00:05:22,238 --> 00:05:26,908
When people were evicted
for a factory development years ago,

98
00:05:26,909 --> 00:05:28,453
the compensation was...

99
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:31,372
What was it? You know...

100
00:05:31,914 --> 00:05:33,791
- Negligible?
- No.

101
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:36,293
- Disappointing?
- No.

102
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:38,337
- Chicken feed!
- That's it.

103
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:43,676
No wonder they're reluctant
to leave their longtime homes.

104
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:49,807
You're the only person
I can ask to do this, Miyaji.

105
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,517
Please.

106
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:55,563
Mr. Motojima, please.
There's no need to bow.

107
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:01,359
All right. I'll speak to my boss...

108
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,819
You'll take the case?

109
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:03,987
I'll speak to her, then...

110
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:05,739
Thank you!

111
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:09,118
Well, I'll leave you to it, then.

112
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:13,122
Goodbye.

113
00:06:14,123 --> 00:06:15,333
Take care.

114
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:19,879
Didn't that...

115
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:22,839
sound like you agreed to take it?

116
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,342
Yes, it certainly sounded that way.

117
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:27,219
We're up against the government.

118
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,179
Doesn't that make this a tough case?

119
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,098
Yeah.

120
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:31,933
Still, we'll find a way...

121
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:35,936
It lists Yasuko Yamaoka
as opposing counsel.

122
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,312
What? Yasuko Yamaoka?

123
00:06:37,313 --> 00:06:38,772
Yes. Right here.

124
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,357
PREPARATORY BRIEF

125
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:42,026
ATTORNEY YASUKO YAMAOKA

126
00:06:45,404 --> 00:06:46,363
Oh, that's bad.

127
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:47,531
Is she a well-known lawyer?

128
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:49,741
What? You don't know her, Ms. Minamida?

129
00:06:49,742 --> 00:06:51,034
No, I don't.

130
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:54,496
She's the managing partner
at MMK Law Firm.

131
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:58,458
Rumor has it she'll follow her father
into politics soon.

132
00:06:58,459 --> 00:06:59,668
She must be very impressive.

133
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:01,254
And that's not all.

134
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:05,632
She and our managing partner
were classmates in college.

135
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:07,802
So just hearing her name

136
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:10,221
gets her all worked up about it.

137
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:15,184
Yasuko Yamaoka, huh?

138
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:20,272
Will your whole team
be working on this, Mr. Miyaji?

139
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:21,565
Yes.

140
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:24,693
There's not much time
until the next hearing.

141
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:27,405
Including Ms. Minamida, then?

142
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:28,823
Yes.

143
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,159
I see...

144
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,327
Don't worry.

145
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:36,998
We have no intention of losing to MMK.

146
00:07:38,249 --> 00:07:40,083
We'll work hard to bring good news.

147
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:41,335
I see.

148
00:07:42,044 --> 00:07:43,129
I'm counting on you.

149
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:44,630
Yes.

150
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:51,512
Well, I said it...

151
00:07:56,851 --> 00:08:00,062
TANEKI RESIDENTS SUE TO HALT
YANOHARA LINE CONSTRUCTION

152
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:20,290
Someone from the plaintiffs'
residents' committee

153
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:22,502
is picking us up here
to take us to Tanegi.

154
00:08:23,961 --> 00:08:25,296
They should be here soon.

155
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,344
THE TANUKI'S PALACE

156
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:35,640
SPECIALTY GRILLED MANJU

157
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:41,187
Yanohara Village seems quite lively.

158
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:43,731
That character seems to be the reason.

159
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,150
"The Tanuki's Palace."

160
00:08:46,734 --> 00:08:48,109
Never heard of it.

161
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:50,947
Apparently, it's a local folktale.

162
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:55,576
So they're revitalizing the village
with a mascot business.

163
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:58,329
Welcome.

164
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:01,082
YANOHARA SAKE CUP

165
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:08,213
Would you like some?
Our Tanuki's Palace cookies are delicious.

166
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,800
Ms. Minamida, read the room.

167
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,300
The room?

168
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:15,428
Those two look good together, don't they?

169
00:09:15,429 --> 00:09:17,557
They clearly like each other.

170
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:21,561
It's good.

171
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,188
I'm glad.

172
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:26,983
You don't understand those things, do you?

173
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:32,113
Excuse me!

174
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:36,032
Are you the lawyers?

175
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:36,992
Yes.

176
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:39,995
I'm Satonaka,
the residents' committee vice chair.

177
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:42,330
Welcome to Taneki Village.

178
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:45,293
Although we're not actually in Taneki yet.

179
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:48,253
Come on, it's right here.

180
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:50,214
It's a bit cramped, but hop in.

181
00:09:56,804 --> 00:09:59,180
Is that a Tanuki's Palace figurine too?

182
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:01,017
Oh, that one.

183
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:02,767
Go ahead. Get in.

184
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:05,354
Excuse me. I'll sit on the far side.

185
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:10,234
Hey. Let those two sit together,
why don't you?

186
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:18,199
Ms. Asahi, please take the far seat.

187
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,077
Huh? Okay.

188
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:30,838
The two of you look good together.

189
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:37,052
The Tanuki's Palace is a folktale
passed down in this area.

190
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:39,929
A fleeing Heike warrior
barely escaped with his life.

191
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:43,558
He was rescued by a tanuki,
which invited him into its home.

192
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:44,810
That's the story.

193
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:50,149
We're entering Taneki Village now.

194
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:54,195
WELCOME TO TANEGI VILLAGE

195
00:10:56,364 --> 00:11:00,242
The railway is supposed
to run through here too.

196
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:02,953
PLANNED RAILWAY SITE

197
00:11:11,545 --> 00:11:12,755
What's that?

198
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,841
That factory closed about 20 years ago.

199
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:19,220
It's been left standing ever since.

200
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,389
When the factory was still operating,

201
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:25,684
the village had a bit more life in it.

202
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:31,231
LOOKOUT HILL

203
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:34,150
From the top of this hill,
you can see the whole village.

204
00:11:34,151 --> 00:11:35,319
Come on. Let's go.

205
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:40,574
Come on. Give it your all
and you'll be up in no time.

206
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:42,326
Right.

207
00:11:45,287 --> 00:11:46,580
You first, Ms. Minamida.

208
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:49,166
No.

209
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:52,503
I would like to walk at the very back.

210
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:55,423
All right.

211
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:03,681
Just three-quarters of the way left!

212
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:08,853
Are you all right?

213
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,022
Yes.

214
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:15,067
It's slippery. Please be careful.

215
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:16,944
Thank you.

216
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:58,860
Ready, and...

217
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,153
WELCOME TO TANEKI VILLAGE

218
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:02,490
Welcome to Taneki Village!

219
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,117
These are our residents'
committee members.

220
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:08,077
Since you were visiting today,

221
00:13:08,078 --> 00:13:09,829
we wanted to welcome you.

222
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,832
We put together a little surprise.

223
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,375
Thank you very much.

224
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:15,793
It's a pleasure to meet you.

225
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:19,714
I'm the mayor of Taneki
and chair of the residents' committee.

226
00:13:19,715 --> 00:13:22,425
I also head our poetry chanting club.

227
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:24,594
Satonaka. Pleased to meet you.

228
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:26,513
I'm Miyaji. A pleasure.

229
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:27,680
Thank you for coming.

230
00:13:27,681 --> 00:13:32,060
This is Mr. Satonaka,
our former school principal.

231
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:33,353
Hello.

232
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:36,189
Next to him is Mr. Satonaka, the barber.

233
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:39,150
And Ms. Satonaka,
who grows mustard spinach.

234
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:41,694
Mr. Satonaka here grows tomatoes.

235
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:44,030
Ms. Satonaka, who has two dogs.

236
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:47,325
And Ms. Satonaka, who has one dog.

237
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:48,451
Other way round.

238
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:50,829
One dog, then two dogs.

239
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:54,082
Well...

240
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:57,085
A lot of people around here
are called Satonaka.

241
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:59,337
So we use nicknames based on jobs

242
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:02,466
or the vegetables people grow.

243
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,681
Is that man also Mr. Satonaka?

244
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:10,599
Huh?

245
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:13,893
That's Kiyoshi.

246
00:14:13,894 --> 00:14:15,563
He doesn't have a nickname?

247
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:18,524
Well, he's a bit...

248
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:29,701
Everyone,

249
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:32,912
you must be getting hungry by now, right?

250
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:35,665
We've brought onigiri.

251
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:38,294
Here, help yourselves. They're delicious.

252
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:49,138
It's delicious.

253
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:53,601
What a beautiful village.

254
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:58,855
I've been climbing this hill
to play since I was a child.

255
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:01,775
The view from here has never changed.

256
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:03,986
If only we still had that...

257
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:06,821
- "That"?
- At Yanohara Station,

258
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:09,365
you saw that
cute tanuki girl character, right?

259
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:11,993
Was it called The Grateful Tanuki?

260
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,370
The Tanuki's Palace.

261
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:20,793
Originally, people said that
that story was set here in Tanegi.

262
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:23,296
Then why is the neighboring
village using it?

263
00:15:23,297 --> 00:15:25,883
It was just over ten years ago.

264
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:31,638
They found a sake cup
with a butterfly design in Yanohara.

265
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:35,725
They examined it and found
it was almost a thousand years old.

266
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:39,437
Apparently, the butterfly
was the Heike clan's crest.

267
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:40,980
I saw that on a poster earlier.

268
00:15:40,981 --> 00:15:42,608
Oh, you saw it, did you?

269
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:45,860
All because they found that one cup,

270
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:49,447
people started saying
The Tanuki's Palace was set in Yanohara.

271
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:51,282
That's what it's become.

272
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:53,242
It was our village's one claim to fame.

273
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:54,161
Right.

274
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:57,957
Everyone here loves this village.

275
00:15:59,124 --> 00:16:00,876
The food is delicious,

276
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,962
and the people are good.

277
00:16:06,006 --> 00:16:09,008
It's not a village
the government should just tear up

278
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:11,595
for its own convenience. Absolutely not.

279
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:13,722
I agree.

280
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:24,190
Well, let's eat.

281
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:26,151
The tomatoes are delicious.

282
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:29,905
All right. Let's give this everything.

283
00:16:30,572 --> 00:16:32,116
We absolutely cannot afford to lose.

284
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,659
Yes!

285
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:37,704
But why did they choose
that particular route?

286
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,581
They could go around the village
instead of through it.

287
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:42,333
To save money, perhaps?

288
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:45,421
A straight line needs less track
than a route around it.

289
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:48,923
If cost was why they rejected
the alternative,

290
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:51,843
it violates the principle
that administrative action

291
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:53,721
must be limited to what is necessary.

292
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:55,346
That's true.

293
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:58,516
But in practice, getting that
overturned is difficult.

294
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:00,476
Especially against Yasuko Yamaoka.

295
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:02,311
Let's look for an opening.

296
00:17:02,312 --> 00:17:05,774
First, let's thoroughly
research this railway project.

297
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:09,527
The documents from Mr. Motojima
have arrived.

298
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:12,531
Well, split it three ways
and it'll be done quickly...

299
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:27,379
I don't think this will be quick.

300
00:17:27,963 --> 00:17:29,465
Well, let's do our best.

301
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:30,924
Yes.

302
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:10,631
ROUTE SELECTION TIMELINE

303
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:19,139
Oh, come on!

304
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:33,027
Deliva Food delivery!

305
00:18:33,028 --> 00:18:34,071
Ririi?

306
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:36,739
Working hard?

307
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:40,869
- No! You can't!
- Huh? What? Okay.

308
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:49,169
There are case files there.
I can't let outsiders in.

309
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:52,880
Your dad asked me to deliver

310
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:54,925
the Minamida Minami Set.

311
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,761
And clothes and your whale sleep aids.

312
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:01,390
I was hungry. Thank you.

313
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:03,350
Ririi.

314
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:05,017
Minato Funai!

315
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:07,770
Oh, these are for your coworkers too.

316
00:19:07,771 --> 00:19:09,231
Onigiri from Beemus.

317
00:19:10,065 --> 00:19:11,441
Thank you very much.

318
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:14,986
I have more documents,
but I can come back if you're busy.

319
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:16,655
No, it's fine! I'll wait.

320
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:18,740
Go right ahead.

321
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:20,742
Excuse me.

322
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:25,788
Please put the additional documents here.

323
00:19:25,789 --> 00:19:27,790
The committee's petition to the prefecture

324
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,209
and the prefecture's reply.

325
00:19:30,752 --> 00:19:32,212
Thank you.

326
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:35,841
Make yourselves comfortable.

327
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:51,899
How are things with Minato Funai?

328
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:53,525
What do you mean?

329
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:55,318
Don't play dumb.

330
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:58,322
I'm asking if you two
have gotten any closer.

331
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:00,990
No.

332
00:20:00,991 --> 00:20:03,242
We haven't gotten any closer.

333
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:05,871
Why not? Doesn't Minato Funai like you?

334
00:20:06,455 --> 00:20:07,580
That's not true.

335
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:08,581
I asked him.

336
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:09,957
You asked him?

337
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:10,876
Yes.

338
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:15,881
He avoided directly addressing
the question.

339
00:20:17,090 --> 00:20:20,927
So I don't think he likes me.

340
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:22,763
When? What did you ask?

341
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:26,390
Minato Funai likes Minami Minamida.

342
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:27,642
Is that true?

343
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:29,186
Well...

344
00:20:29,853 --> 00:20:32,022
For a member of staff,

345
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:35,317
that's a difficult question.

346
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:38,236
That's a straight-up interrogation.

347
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:39,528
If you ask like that,

348
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:41,406
no one's going to say, "Yes, it's true."

349
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:47,495
But Minato and Ms. Asahi
look good together.

350
00:20:47,496 --> 00:20:50,249
Ms. Asahi? The one with the tiny face?

351
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:51,667
Yes.

352
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,543
It's good.

353
00:20:54,419 --> 00:20:55,629
I'm glad.

354
00:20:57,547 --> 00:21:00,425
So? You don't feel anything about that?

355
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:13,355
It feels as if my chest is being squeezed
into a salted onigiri.

356
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:15,231
It feels strange.

357
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:16,608
That's jealousy.

358
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,025
Jealousy?

359
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:19,527
Yeah. The green-eyed monster.

360
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:21,655
It means you like
Minato Funai, doesn't it?

361
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:27,661
I'm not really sure.

362
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:30,830
If you're not sure whether you like him,

363
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:33,249
try making physical contact with Minato.

364
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,208
What?

365
00:21:34,209 --> 00:21:37,671
If you like someone,
your heart rate shoots up.

366
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,798
No. I can't do something like that...

367
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:42,508
Then make up an excuse.

368
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:44,343
Say, "Let me read your palm."

369
00:21:44,344 --> 00:21:46,053
If your heart starts going crazy

370
00:21:46,054 --> 00:21:48,889
and it pounds so hard
you think it'll burst,

371
00:21:48,890 --> 00:21:50,892
then you definitely like him.

372
00:22:02,612 --> 00:22:04,406
- Excuse me.
- Thank you.

373
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:08,159
Thanks for all your hard work
on such short notice.

374
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,203
Did you find any grounds for illegality?

375
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:13,956
We barely got through
the documents, so not yet.

376
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:15,833
Rather than looking for illegality,

377
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:17,626
could we try a different approach?

378
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:19,003
Such as?

379
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:21,964
I reviewed the two other routes
in the original plan

380
00:22:21,965 --> 00:22:24,592
to see why neither of them was chosen.

381
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:27,053
On the proposed route along the bypass,

382
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:29,139
the prefectural assembly speaker
has a home.

383
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:31,224
Just water is okay, right?

384
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:33,768
If that route had been selected,

385
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:35,811
his house would have had to be vacated.

386
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:38,314
Could they have been
trying to accommodate him?

387
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:42,109
Hard to say.
Evidence would make a difference.

388
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:44,071
- Do you have a map?
- Yes.

389
00:22:46,406 --> 00:22:48,075
It's rather large.

390
00:23:03,548 --> 00:23:04,633
Right here.

391
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:08,470
Yes, it is on the proposed route.

392
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:11,515
Good find, Mr. Himi.

393
00:23:12,682 --> 00:23:15,017
We've no other leads.
Let's all take another look

394
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:16,477
to see if that angle could work.

395
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:17,562
Yes.

396
00:23:24,694 --> 00:23:26,571
What are you doing, Ms. Minamida?

397
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:31,326
Well...

398
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:33,953
I was wondering about Minato's palm lines...

399
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:35,162
What?

400
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:37,541
Why now? Isn't your timing a bit off?

401
00:23:39,126 --> 00:23:40,168
I'm sorry.

402
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:43,796
ROUTE SELECTION TIMELINE

403
00:23:43,797 --> 00:23:45,632
JUNE 2023: STRATEGIC ENVIRONMENTAL REVIEW

404
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:47,717
The timing of it...

405
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:04,024
The timing is wrong!

406
00:24:04,025 --> 00:24:06,443
Yes, I was discussing the other routes.

407
00:24:06,444 --> 00:24:10,531
Yes. That's how I realized
the timing is wrong.

408
00:24:10,532 --> 00:24:13,117
This makes the route selection unlawful.

409
00:24:13,118 --> 00:24:14,578
- What?
- How so?

410
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:18,706
It violates strategic environmental
assessment requirements.

411
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:21,458
But the assessments were all completed...

412
00:24:21,459 --> 00:24:24,670
Yes, but the issue is
when they were conducted.

413
00:24:24,671 --> 00:24:27,923
The prefectural ordinance
requires a strategic

414
00:24:27,924 --> 00:24:31,594
environmental assessment
at the planning stage of projects

415
00:24:31,595 --> 00:24:34,430
that could have an environmental impact.

416
00:24:34,431 --> 00:24:39,226
In this case, the construction
plan was drawn up in 2021,

417
00:24:39,227 --> 00:24:43,272
but the strategic environmental
assessment was done in 2023.

418
00:24:43,273 --> 00:24:45,482
That's a serious legal violation.

419
00:24:45,483 --> 00:24:46,775
Well spotted, Ms. Minamida.

420
00:24:46,776 --> 00:24:48,652
Put it in a preparatory brief now.

421
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:49,570
Yes!

422
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:51,739
What about favoring the assembly speaker...?

423
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:54,951
We're short on time.
Let's prioritize Ms. Minamida's finding.

424
00:24:56,077 --> 00:24:58,330
Right. Excellent work. Well done.

425
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:11,217
Excuse me.

426
00:25:11,218 --> 00:25:14,678
Opposing counsel sent their brief
for the next hearing.

427
00:25:14,679 --> 00:25:15,805
Thank you.

428
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:18,724
PREPARATORY BRIEF

429
00:25:18,725 --> 00:25:19,642
KENGO MIYAJI

430
00:25:19,643 --> 00:25:22,728
So the opposing counsel has changed
to Hirokawa & Howard.

431
00:25:22,729 --> 00:25:23,855
That's right.

432
00:25:24,606 --> 00:25:25,440
I see.

433
00:25:35,575 --> 00:25:38,411
HIROKAWA & HOWARD LAW FIRM
HIMI, ASAHI, MINAMIDA

434
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:49,588
COURTHOUSE

435
00:25:49,589 --> 00:25:50,673
Mr. Miyaji.

436
00:25:50,674 --> 00:25:52,049
THIRD ORAL ARGUMENT HEARING

437
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,093
Thank you.

438
00:25:53,635 --> 00:25:54,678
She's not here.

439
00:25:55,262 --> 00:25:56,846
Yasuko Yamaoka?

440
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:34,801
Of course we'd face her.

441
00:26:35,885 --> 00:26:38,096
She has quite a presence in person.

442
00:26:51,901 --> 00:26:54,696
All right. Let's focus on the hearing.

443
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:05,497
Under the prefecture's
assessment ordinance,

444
00:27:05,498 --> 00:27:07,666
a strategic environmental assessment

445
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:11,003
should be conducted
when the project is planned.

446
00:27:11,004 --> 00:27:12,004
In this case,

447
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:15,883
although the railway's basic design
was completed in 2021,

448
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:17,593
it was not done until 2023.

449
00:27:17,594 --> 00:27:19,929
The timing is therefore problematic.

450
00:27:20,513 --> 00:27:21,514
Your Honor.

451
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:24,392
Defense counsel. Go ahead.

452
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:30,731
When you choose a house
or an apartment to live in,

453
00:27:30,732 --> 00:27:32,233
what do you consider?

454
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:37,988
Cost and layout matter,
but barring special circumstances,

455
00:27:37,989 --> 00:27:39,490
before settling on a property,

456
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:41,617
you check the neighborhood

457
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:44,913
and find out where the nearest
station and hospital are.

458
00:27:46,414 --> 00:27:48,665
You don't want
to choose a home, then regret it

459
00:27:48,666 --> 00:27:51,294
because there's no supermarket nearby
and shopping is a pain.

460
00:27:55,382 --> 00:27:57,174
Plaintiffs' counsel is arguing

461
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:59,301
that checking for a supermarket

462
00:27:59,302 --> 00:28:02,430
two years after thinking of moving
makes no sense.

463
00:28:03,014 --> 00:28:04,265
That is certainly true.

464
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:06,934
However, what matters

465
00:28:06,935 --> 00:28:10,687
is when the decision was made,
not when planning began.

466
00:28:10,688 --> 00:28:12,107
Please take a look at this.

467
00:28:15,151 --> 00:28:19,364
The optimal route
was selected in October 2023.

468
00:28:20,365 --> 00:28:22,574
The strategic environmental assessment

469
00:28:22,575 --> 00:28:24,953
was conducted that June,
four months earlier.

470
00:28:25,578 --> 00:28:27,121
Before choosing the property,

471
00:28:27,122 --> 00:28:29,457
they did check where the supermarket was.

472
00:28:32,919 --> 00:28:36,296
It is true that
the assessment was delayed.

473
00:28:36,297 --> 00:28:39,717
But it was completed
before the plan was finalized.

474
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:41,302
There was no violation.

475
00:28:45,306 --> 00:28:46,683
What is it?

476
00:28:50,061 --> 00:28:52,271
The committee's petition to the prefecture

477
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:53,481
and the prefecture's reply.

478
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:58,653
That's incorrect!

479
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:01,405
What is?

480
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:03,907
If defense counsel's argument is correct,

481
00:29:03,908 --> 00:29:05,993
the route could have been changed

482
00:29:05,994 --> 00:29:07,954
until October 2023.

483
00:29:08,538 --> 00:29:10,539
However, please look
at Plaintiff's Exhibit 4,

484
00:29:10,540 --> 00:29:12,875
the reply sent by the prefecture
in the governor's name

485
00:29:12,876 --> 00:29:16,044
to the Taneki Village Residents' Committee

486
00:29:16,045 --> 00:29:16,963
What?

487
00:29:21,468 --> 00:29:24,262
Under the third item...

488
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:26,055
The second line.

489
00:29:26,973 --> 00:29:30,476
It says the preliminary
and detailed designs were complete,

490
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:32,896
making a change of route impossible.

491
00:29:34,689 --> 00:29:36,106
Yes, it does.

492
00:29:36,107 --> 00:29:39,151
As of April 2023,
the prefecture had replied

493
00:29:39,152 --> 00:29:41,945
that the route could no longer be changed.

494
00:29:41,946 --> 00:29:46,200
In that case,
plaintiffs' counsel's claim that

495
00:29:46,201 --> 00:29:49,370
the strategic environmental assessment
came too late is valid.

496
00:29:51,831 --> 00:29:53,082
Well said!

497
00:30:02,967 --> 00:30:06,011
Certainly, the procedural shortcomings
in this case

498
00:30:06,012 --> 00:30:09,557
may have affected
the comparative assessment of the options.

499
00:30:10,141 --> 00:30:14,812
However, the decision to adopt this plan
was based on profitability, safety,

500
00:30:14,813 --> 00:30:16,522
potential for future development,

501
00:30:16,523 --> 00:30:19,316
and a comprehensive review
of all other factors.

502
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:23,362
Furthermore, the strategic
environmental assessment

503
00:30:23,363 --> 00:30:26,240
did not find that the plan failed
to adequately avoid

504
00:30:26,241 --> 00:30:29,160
or mitigate serious environmental impacts.

505
00:30:30,286 --> 00:30:34,456
Moreover, this project serves the public
by improving residents' transport access

506
00:30:34,457 --> 00:30:37,167
and revitalizing the area
by attracting tourists.

507
00:30:37,168 --> 00:30:40,171
It is being pursued
for these substantial public benefits.

508
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:46,385
Under these circumstances,
does a procedural flaw alone

509
00:30:46,386 --> 00:30:49,096
amount to illegality serious enough

510
00:30:49,097 --> 00:30:54,060
to overturn the entire plan
when construction is already underway?

511
00:31:29,512 --> 00:31:30,346
Here.

512
00:31:31,556 --> 00:31:32,515
Thank you.

513
00:31:36,102 --> 00:31:37,061
Um...

514
00:31:41,816 --> 00:31:43,610
Thank you for earlier too.

515
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:45,987
Likewise.

516
00:31:47,238 --> 00:31:49,740
My name is Minami Minamida.

517
00:31:49,741 --> 00:31:52,367
Forwards or backwards,
I'm Minami Minamida.

518
00:31:52,368 --> 00:31:56,039
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic,
racecar, Minami Minamida.

519
00:31:59,876 --> 00:32:02,670
I have autism spectrum disorder.

520
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:07,215
My father tells me not to say unnecessary
things when introducing myself,

521
00:32:07,216 --> 00:32:08,468
but I can't help it.

522
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:09,928
I see.

523
00:32:14,807 --> 00:32:16,768
I hope we get along.

524
00:32:19,437 --> 00:32:20,480
Yes.

525
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:28,570
Of course.

526
00:32:28,571 --> 00:32:31,407
For now, we are opponents
fighting each other.

527
00:32:34,994 --> 00:32:37,246
You have a remarkable memory.

528
00:32:37,914 --> 00:32:39,374
I was very impressed.

529
00:32:39,999 --> 00:32:41,542
You were impressed?

530
00:32:43,086 --> 00:32:44,087
Well, then.

531
00:32:44,587 --> 00:32:46,881
I'll see you at the next hearing.

532
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:04,816
Thank you very much.

533
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:07,734
This in the front seat?

534
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:09,320
I'll take that.

535
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:15,243
What did you discuss with Ms. Yamaoka?

536
00:33:15,743 --> 00:33:18,453
First meeting, and you flatter her?

537
00:33:18,454 --> 00:33:20,122
You're good at selling yourself.

538
00:33:20,123 --> 00:33:21,707
I wasn't selling myself.

539
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:24,001
I can take one of you back to the office.

540
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:25,336
Right. Well, then...

541
00:33:32,218 --> 00:33:33,970
Ms. Minamida, would you like a ride?

542
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:36,097
No, thank you.

543
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:38,724
Ms. Asahi, please go.

544
00:33:38,725 --> 00:33:40,143
What? Me?

545
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:48,609
Minato and you look good together.

546
00:33:55,199 --> 00:33:56,324
May I?

547
00:33:56,325 --> 00:33:57,785
Of course.

548
00:33:58,369 --> 00:33:59,328
Well, then.

549
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,434
Excuse me.

550
00:34:22,185 --> 00:34:23,728
Shall we get going?

551
00:34:25,313 --> 00:34:28,816
Actually... I'll take the train back.

552
00:34:29,609 --> 00:34:30,568
Huh?

553
00:34:32,195 --> 00:34:34,989
Being alone with you... is difficult.

554
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:38,659
Wait, Ms. Asahi!

555
00:34:41,204 --> 00:34:42,454
Did I...

556
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:46,876
do something that upset you, Ms. Asahi?

557
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:50,463
Yes, you did.

558
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:53,257
What... did I do?

559
00:34:54,717 --> 00:34:57,678
Catching me when I nearly fell,

560
00:34:58,846 --> 00:35:00,765
taking my hand on that hill...

561
00:35:02,183 --> 00:35:05,311
You're just so kind, Mr. Funai.

562
00:35:05,978 --> 00:35:06,854
Huh?

563
00:35:08,606 --> 00:35:09,856
Mr. Funai,

564
00:35:09,857 --> 00:35:13,236
you still listen to Ms. Minamida
talk about whales, right?

565
00:35:14,195 --> 00:35:15,113
Yes.

566
00:35:15,947 --> 00:35:17,781
Why do you do that?

567
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:20,367
Is it because you want to listen?

568
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:24,747
Or is it because Ms. Minamida
wants to tell you about them?

569
00:35:26,332 --> 00:35:27,834
Both, I suppose.

570
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:31,254
Even your answer is kind!

571
00:35:33,381 --> 00:35:34,882
Being kind like that...

572
00:35:35,883 --> 00:35:38,135
ends up hurting all sorts of people.

573
00:35:38,136 --> 00:35:40,054
It gives people the wrong idea.

574
00:35:41,097 --> 00:35:43,808
Ms. Minamida, Mr. Himi,

575
00:35:45,476 --> 00:35:46,811
and me too...

576
00:35:49,105 --> 00:35:51,524
We all got the wrong idea, didn't we?

577
00:35:52,733 --> 00:35:55,277
What... should I do, then?

578
00:35:55,278 --> 00:35:56,862
That's the problem.

579
00:35:56,863 --> 00:35:59,323
You don't have to be so considerate.

580
00:36:00,199 --> 00:36:01,325
But...

581
00:36:03,077 --> 00:36:04,370
Mr. Funai...

582
00:36:06,622 --> 00:36:07,957
that's what I like about you.

583
00:36:10,501 --> 00:36:11,669
Honestly...

584
00:36:12,503 --> 00:36:13,671
Excuse me.

585
00:36:29,729 --> 00:36:30,938
I'm coming in.

586
00:36:33,274 --> 00:36:34,734
Aren't you having dinner?

587
00:36:40,406 --> 00:36:41,991
MMK - YASUKO YAMAOKA
MANAGING PARTNER

588
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:43,618
What's that?

589
00:36:45,411 --> 00:36:46,370
Dad.

590
00:36:46,913 --> 00:36:49,539
Do you know a lawyer named Yasuko Yamaoka?

591
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:51,791
She graduated
from Tokyo University's law faculty,

592
00:36:51,792 --> 00:36:54,212
so you might have met her yourself.

593
00:36:54,962 --> 00:36:56,339
Why are you researching her?

594
00:36:57,006 --> 00:36:59,633
She is opposing counsel
in the case I am handling.

595
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:00,550
What?

596
00:37:00,551 --> 00:37:02,177
I saw her in court today.

597
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:03,763
She was very impressive.

598
00:37:04,388 --> 00:37:05,681
She explained the law

599
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:09,477
clearly using examples of moving
and supermarkets.

600
00:37:10,853 --> 00:37:14,148
I want to be like Ms. Yamaoka.

601
00:37:27,995 --> 00:37:29,705
MANAGING PARTNER
NAGISA HIROKAWA

602
00:37:36,254 --> 00:37:39,131
Sorry to keep you waiting, Makoto.

603
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:42,426
I have an appointment after this,
so I don't have much time.

604
00:37:45,388 --> 00:37:47,598
What is it? Is something wrong?

605
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:51,769
The case Minami is working on now...

606
00:37:52,395 --> 00:37:54,062
I heard the lawyer on the other side

607
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:56,065
is Yasuko Yamaoka.

608
00:37:58,150 --> 00:38:01,862
Why did you hire Minami
to work at your firm?

609
00:38:04,490 --> 00:38:06,032
Why? Well...

610
00:38:06,033 --> 00:38:07,993
You rejected her application once.

611
00:38:07,994 --> 00:38:10,997
Hiring her six months later
isn't exactly normal.

612
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:13,499
You knew, didn't you?

613
00:38:14,542 --> 00:38:16,294
Who Minami's mother is.

614
00:38:21,882 --> 00:38:23,175
Back in college,

615
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:26,177
I had a feeling that you and Yasuko

616
00:38:26,178 --> 00:38:28,055
were dating each other.

617
00:38:28,639 --> 00:38:31,976
When I heard that you had a daughter,

618
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:34,353
I did think, "Could she be..."

619
00:38:35,229 --> 00:38:38,481
Since she still hadn't found a position,

620
00:38:38,482 --> 00:38:40,276
- I offered her a job.
- That's not it.

621
00:38:42,611 --> 00:38:44,530
You hired Minami

622
00:38:45,197 --> 00:38:47,575
because you thought
you could use her, didn't you?

623
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:49,993
What?

624
00:38:49,994 --> 00:38:52,580
There's talk of Yasuko entering politics.

625
00:38:53,247 --> 00:38:54,789
If that happens,

626
00:38:54,790 --> 00:38:57,959
MMK, already the top firm,
will gain even more momentum.

627
00:38:57,960 --> 00:39:00,421
The gap with Hirokawa & Howard
will keep widening.

628
00:39:01,380 --> 00:39:02,381
So...

629
00:39:03,257 --> 00:39:05,633
you decided to bring Yasuko Yamaoka down

630
00:39:05,634 --> 00:39:08,596
by using the scandal
of her secret daughter.

631
00:39:09,096 --> 00:39:09,930
Am I wrong?

632
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:16,312
What an active imagination.

633
00:39:17,355 --> 00:39:19,689
You know I'd never do anything like that.

634
00:39:19,690 --> 00:39:20,774
How can you be so sure?

635
00:39:20,775 --> 00:39:22,234
How? Well...

636
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:25,196
Then what would you do if that were true?

637
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:27,280
Make your daughter leave the firm?

638
00:39:27,281 --> 00:39:29,408
I would if I could!

639
00:39:30,910 --> 00:39:33,120
She graduated top of her class

640
00:39:33,746 --> 00:39:36,748
and scored highest on the bar exam,
but she's autistic,

641
00:39:36,749 --> 00:39:39,085
so not one firm would even
give her an interview.

642
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:41,379
After all that,

643
00:39:41,879 --> 00:39:45,257
this firm was the chance
she finally managed to get.

644
00:39:46,675 --> 00:39:48,051
So I'm begging you.

645
00:39:48,052 --> 00:39:49,969
Don't use Minami.

646
00:39:49,970 --> 00:39:52,473
Please let her
keep working here as she is.

647
00:39:53,307 --> 00:39:55,475
I know I'm asking to have it both ways.

648
00:39:55,476 --> 00:39:57,645
Please. I'm begging you!

649
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:01,023
Makoto...

650
00:40:08,948 --> 00:40:10,908
Managing Partner, it's nearly time.

651
00:40:14,954 --> 00:40:16,080
I'm sorry.

652
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:20,334
I have to go now.

653
00:40:37,643 --> 00:40:38,769
Dad?

654
00:40:40,312 --> 00:40:41,355
Oh, Minami.

655
00:40:41,939 --> 00:40:42,772
"Dad"?

656
00:40:42,773 --> 00:40:45,525
I know someone here,
so I came to see them.

657
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:46,569
I'm heading home.

658
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:48,112
Hello.

659
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:58,830
How does your father know
the managing partner, Ms. Minamida?

660
00:40:58,831 --> 00:41:00,416
He came out of her office.

661
00:41:01,417 --> 00:41:02,751
Yes, he did.

662
00:41:03,335 --> 00:41:04,169
Wait...

663
00:41:04,170 --> 00:41:06,004
I read something online before.

664
00:41:06,005 --> 00:41:09,632
Your father used to want
to become a lawyer, didn't he?

665
00:41:09,633 --> 00:41:11,092
Which university did he attend?

666
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:13,137
Tokyo University's law faculty.

667
00:41:18,350 --> 00:41:21,270
I see. That explains it.

668
00:41:22,646 --> 00:41:23,730
Explains what?

669
00:41:23,731 --> 00:41:26,608
Well, it's pretty obvious... Right?

670
00:41:26,609 --> 00:41:27,942
Please explain.

671
00:41:27,943 --> 00:41:32,489
Our managing partner also graduated
from Tokyo University's law faculty.

672
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:35,910
They were at college together.
He was her senior.

673
00:41:37,953 --> 00:41:41,332
That's how you got hired
by this firm, Ms. Minamida.

674
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:43,166
What?

675
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:46,629
Through your father's connections,
not your own ability.

676
00:41:47,796 --> 00:41:50,758
Your hiring was improper, Ms. Minamida.

677
00:42:01,852 --> 00:42:02,978
Welcome home.

678
00:42:04,104 --> 00:42:06,481
Why were you meeting
with the managing partner?

679
00:42:06,482 --> 00:42:08,608
How do you know the managing partner?

680
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:09,693
Oh, that.

681
00:42:10,569 --> 00:42:11,654
Well, you see...

682
00:42:13,489 --> 00:42:15,281
The head of your firm...

683
00:42:15,282 --> 00:42:17,576
She was my junior at university.

684
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:22,121
Did I get into the firm
because of your connections?

685
00:42:22,122 --> 00:42:23,331
Was I improperly hired?

686
00:42:23,332 --> 00:42:24,416
Well...

687
00:42:25,709 --> 00:42:27,962
Adults have
all kinds of things to deal with.

688
00:42:28,462 --> 00:42:30,464
You don't need to worry about it, okay?

689
00:42:31,090 --> 00:42:34,342
I've had a proper talk
with the managing partner.

690
00:42:34,343 --> 00:42:35,594
Don't worry.

691
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:41,892
Why would you do something like that?

692
00:42:44,103 --> 00:42:45,688
I'm an adult too.

693
00:42:46,897 --> 00:42:49,316
Please stop treating me like a child.

694
00:42:50,192 --> 00:42:52,443
I'm trying to protect you from setbacks...

695
00:42:52,444 --> 00:42:54,989
I want to experience setbacks for myself.

696
00:42:56,448 --> 00:42:57,658
What?

697
00:42:59,034 --> 00:43:02,621
You always step into my life
and interfere,

698
00:43:03,122 --> 00:43:05,332
so I can't even fail on my own.

699
00:43:07,293 --> 00:43:09,878
Please stop interfering
when I haven't asked you to!

700
00:43:10,754 --> 00:43:11,839
Minami!

701
00:43:34,737 --> 00:43:36,614
Minami, listen to me.

702
00:43:43,037 --> 00:43:44,788
I'm moving out.

703
00:43:45,372 --> 00:43:46,205
What are you saying?

704
00:43:46,206 --> 00:43:49,501
I'll live on my own without your help.

705
00:43:50,085 --> 00:43:52,212
Minami. Wait a minute! Minami!

706
00:43:54,548 --> 00:43:55,466
Minami!

707
00:44:13,525 --> 00:44:14,693
Dad?

708
00:44:24,745 --> 00:44:26,330
TO EVERYONE AT HIROKAWA & HOWARD

709
00:44:27,873 --> 00:44:30,167
IMPROPER HIRING

710
00:44:32,086 --> 00:44:33,879
I HEREBY EXPOSE

711
00:44:35,798 --> 00:44:38,926
TO EVERYONE: I HEREBY EXPOSE
IMPROPER HIRING AT HIROKAWA & HOWARD.

712
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:49,769
Subtitle translation by:
Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

713
00:44:49,770 --> 00:44:52,647
<i>Should such improper conduct
really be tolerated?</i>

714
00:44:52,648 --> 00:44:53,856
<i>It makes me so angry.</i>

715
00:44:53,857 --> 00:44:55,900
- You should punch him.
- Take that!

716
00:44:55,901 --> 00:44:56,819
What are you doing?

717
00:44:57,403 --> 00:44:58,445
<i>I realized...</i>

718
00:44:59,279 --> 00:45:00,489
<i>how I feel about Minato...</i>

719
00:45:01,698 --> 00:45:04,325
- Funai can draft the consent form.

720
00:45:04,326 --> 00:45:06,662
- It has nothing do with you.
- Yes, it is!

721
00:45:07,871 --> 00:45:08,831
Excuse me!

722
00:45:10,541 --> 00:45:12,834
There is nothing... I can tell you.

723
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:13,794
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
